                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2e99fda9-2d28-4e76-91c2-12c75a995aee",
                        "entry_id": "ba43dba0-a12f-36a4-901c-439b88d9bedd",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "caliches"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cf5931bb-e6a0-3598-b8e6-5a8beae91409",
                        "entry_id": "ba43dba0-a12f-36a4-901c-439b88d9bedd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Roche carbonatée dont on extrait le nitrate de sodium. On le trouve surtout au Chili."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8afb4f6b-4b20-4c56-9660-7a5e88b9f7d9",
                                "sense_id": "cf5931bb-e6a0-3598-b8e6-5a8beae91409",
                                "text": "L’analyse de la terre à salpêtre ou caliche [découverte à Arica, Pérou] a donné des résultats favorables."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6be0a679-65fc-4956-8f79-5c666dc07f41",
                                "sense_id": "cf5931bb-e6a0-3598-b8e6-5a8beae91409",
                                "text": "Puis vient le caliche qui est la couche la plus riche en nitrate et autres composants."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "13e4a86b-a8fc-4fa0-ab93-f6d55f733867",
                                "sense_id": "cf5931bb-e6a0-3598-b8e6-5a8beae91409",
                                "text": "Chez moi c’est Moody County dans le sud du Texas, là où les plaines des blacklands viennent buter contre les collines de caliche."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1b296d5b-ca1b-4e9c-9067-1d544391922a",
                        "source_entry_id": "ba43dba0-a12f-36a4-901c-439b88d9bedd",
                        "source_sense_id": "cf5931bb-e6a0-3598-b8e6-5a8beae91409",
                        "target_lang_word": "caliche",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "caliche",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5a97d736-4d6b-38ac-9b52-63bfa9420ed7",
                                        "entry_id": "35be428f-8d46-3343-9df1-3a256eb2b3d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A crude form of sodium nitrate from South America; used as a fertilizer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1f07b0cb-a3b6-366d-9111-4acf2f59d7f3",
                                        "entry_id": "35be428f-8d46-3343-9df1-3a256eb2b3d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A layer of hard clay subsoil or sedimentary rock; hardpan."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8a46845-d2d9-48d0-9743-1a08fa416858",
                                                "sense_id": "1f07b0cb-a3b6-366d-9111-4acf2f59d7f3",
                                                "text": "According to local well drillers, in wells drilled on the high plains a few hundred feet back from the caliche escarpment or in other locations on the high plains in this area no hard caliche or white layer, such as would characterize a soft layer of high lime-carbonate content, is generally reached at a depth corresponding to the elevation of the caliche escarpment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a07c40cc-c91a-4963-a8db-34ba4d34841b",
                                                "sense_id": "1f07b0cb-a3b6-366d-9111-4acf2f59d7f3",
                                                "text": "Having a layer of caliche at depths of 16 inches and less really puts a damper on the garden site. The caliche does not allow roots to penetrate it (tree roots often take 10 years to break through a caliche layer) nor does this mineral allow water to drain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "415df7b1-5b44-4521-b351-962fc355c9ae",
                                                "sense_id": "1f07b0cb-a3b6-366d-9111-4acf2f59d7f3",
                                                "text": "Caliche in various forms, namely powdery, nodule, tube, fracture-infill, laminar crust, hard laminated crust (hardpan) and pisolitic crust, is widespread in the Mersin area in southern Turkey (Eren et al., 2008; Kadir and Eren, 2008)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
